\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Overview of the positive-control design. We plant known-misaligned anchors with matched aligned controls in three domains, run one fixed battery of standard detectors on every item with identical inputs, and report sensitivity per domain. A rubric ablation on the two subtle domains tests whether a domain-appropriate rubric, or a reference answer, recovers the anchors.}}{2}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:overview}{{1}{2}{Overview of the positive-control design. We plant known-misaligned anchors with matched aligned controls in three domains, run one fixed battery of standard detectors on every item with identical inputs, and report sensitivity per domain. A rubric ablation on the two subtle domains tests whether a domain-appropriate rubric, or a reference answer, recovers the anchors}{figure.1}{}}
